RED confirmed — the guard precisely pins both construction sites (`js_app_view.dart:833` and it will list the tile one too). 

Now write the behavioral tests (also RED — they'll fail to compile since `voxelWorld` getter doesn't exist, which is fine for TDD but let me focus: the guideline wants a failing repro test; the guard is the primary repro. The behavioral tests will be validated GREEN after the fix).

Now implement the fix (GREEN):

1. `js_app_engine.dart` — add the getter + one-shot diagnostic helper.

Let me design the diagnostic helper carefully. Requirements (AC3):
- One-line diagnostic logged when a tree with a voxel node is rendered while `voxelWorld == null`.
- One-shot (no spam per frame).
- Testable via AppLog.

Where do the surfaces call it? In both files right before/at renderer construction:

```dart
engine.noteMissingVoxelWorld(tree);
```

Hmm, naming. Maybe `diagnoseVoxelWorld(tree)`? Or keep it simple and self-explanatory: `warnIfVoxelWorldUnwired(tree)`. Let me write it on JsAppEngine:

```dart
/// Whether the one-shot unwired-voxel diagnostic already fired (see
/// [noteUnwiredVoxelWorld]).
bool _voxelDiagnosticShown = false;

/// gh-1441 AC3: a tree carrying a `voxel` node while this engine has NO
/// voxel world renders the renderer's "Voxel world" placeholder —
/// indistinguishable from a broken widget unless the host says why. A
/// minimal custom backend can ship no world (JsWidgetEngine.voxelWorld is
/// null there); shipped backends always have one, so on them this never
/// fires. Logs ONCE per engine instance.
void noteUnwiredVoxelWorld(Map<String, dynamic> tree) {
  if (_voxelDiagnosticShown || voxelWorld != null) return;
  if (!_containsVoxelNode(tree)) return;
  _voxelDiagnosticShown = true;
  AppLog.i(
    'apps',
    'WARNING: ${app.id}/$entryFile: voxel node in tree but no voxelWorld '
        'wired on this surface — the bridge world is missing (minimal '
        'backend?); the "Voxel world" placeholder is the host wiring, not '
        'a broken widget',
  );
}

static bool _containsVoxelNode(Map<String, dynamic> node) { ... recursive ... }
```

The recursive walk: node map values may be `Map`, `List` of maps. Walk children keys commonly `children`, `rows`, `columns`, `actions`... Rather than enumerating keys, walk ALL values: for each value, if Map with a 'type' == 'voxel' → true; recurse into Map and List values. Depth-capped to avoid pathological trees (say 64). That's simple and generic.

Wait — one consideration: is a *public* method on JsAppEngine the right surface? The alternative: duplicate a tiny helper in each file — worse (duplication). The engine is the shared object both sites hold. Public API addition is small and documented. OK.

2. `js_app_view.dart` — in `_treeView`:
```dart
final renderer = JsonWidgetRenderer(
  ...
  // Voxel nodes: the bridge-owned world the engine's backend created at
  // start — the SAME world `voxel.*` hostCalls land in (see JsAppEngine).
  // Without it every `voxel` node degrades to the "Voxel world"
  // placeholder (gh-1441).
  voxelWorld: engine.voxelWorld,
  ...
);
// gh-1441 AC3: ... diagnostic for null-world surfaces
engine.noteUnwiredVoxelWorld(tree);
```

Where to call noteUnwiredVoxelWorld — before build. It's cheap (returns immediately when world != null).

3. `dynamic_widget_tile.dart` — same in the canvas build.

Let me now write the edits. First read the exact regions with hashline to edit precisely. I'll use exact-match edits.

Edit 1 — js_app_engine.dart near exportedState/peekLogs (line ~366):
```dart
  Map<String, dynamic>? get exportedState => _engine?.exportedState;
  List<Map<String, dynamic>> peekLogs() => _engine?.peekLogs() ?? const [];
```
Add after it the getter + helper. Need `AppLog` import — check existing imports in js_app_engine.dart (it uses AppLog.i already — yes, `AppLog.i('apps', 'engine start: ...')`). Good.

Also need `JsVoxelWorld` type — js_widget_engine.dart exports? js_app_engine.dart imports `package:js_widget_runtime/js_widget_runtime.dart` presumably. Let me check imports.

